// ITEM PACKS (OSRS). A pack is bought from a shop and opened for 100 of something, which saves
// buying that something 28 slots at a time. Post-2006 content, so under the era rule these are
// ported to behave exactly as Old School has them rather than reinvented, and nothing 2006-era
// changes to make room for them.
//
// Every field below was read out of a modern OSRS cache with tools/models/importosrs.py --dry-run,
// which decodes the cache record rather than transcribing a wiki table: name, desc, the 2d icon
// angles, the recolours, weight, cost and the Open op are the cache's own.
//
// The two exceptions, both because the cache field the importer reads is not the wiki's answer:
//   * tradeable - the importer emits tradeable=no when the cache record carries no tradeable flag
//     it can decode. The Water-filled vial pack's own wiki page says tradeable = Yes and noteable =
//     Yes, so the line is dropped (the build's default is tradeable) and a cert record added.
//   * category and param= - the importer cannot know these; they are what makes Open work. See
//     item_packs.param.

[water_filled_vial_pack]
name=Water-filled vial pack
desc=A pack containing 100 vials of water.
model=obj_water_filled_vial_pack
2dzoom=1411
2dyan=2047
2dxof=-3
2dyof=-3
recol1s=25231
recol1d=18788
recol2s=27345
recol2d=13540
recol3s=22060
recol3d=18788
weight=2100g
cost=201
iop1=Open
category=item_pack
param=item_pack_contents,cert_vial_water
param=item_pack_amount,100

[cert_water_filled_vial_pack]
certlink=water_filled_vial_pack
certtemplate=template_for_cert

// THE FIVE ELEMENTAL RUNE PACKS (OSRS, 18 September 2014, "Bounty Hunter"). Same treatment as the
// vial pack above: objs 12728 / 12730 / 12732 / 12734 / 12736 in a modern OSRS cache, read out with
// tools/models/importosrs.py --dry-run, so the names, examines, 2d icon angles, weights and costs
// are the cache's own. None of the five models was already in the build under another name - all
// five were checked by hash against every obj model here before any was imported - so they took
// model ids 24601-24605.
//
// THE SIXTH ONE IS MISSING ON PURPOSE. Old School sells a chaos rune pack (obj 12738) beside these
// five in every shop below, and it is deliberately NOT here. It is a 9,950gp item that puts 100
// chaos runes in a player's hand in one click, which is a real lever on a 2006 rune economy in a
// way five packs of cheap elementals are not; the owner weighed that and chose to leave it out.
// So the shop blocks in all.inv are the OSRS tables with the chaos column dropped, and they are
// not incomplete. Anyone "completing the set" later is reversing a decision, not fixing an
// oversight. The TzHaar variants (21698/21701/21704/21707) and the Last Man Standing packs
// (Elemental 20524, Catalytic 20523, both removed from Old School in 2019 and unobtainable) are
// out for their own reasons and were never in scope.
//
// Unlike the vial pack these hand over UNNOTED runes: the OSRS wiki's Item pack page says a pack's
// contents come out noted "unless the item is already stackable", and every rune here is
// stackable=yes, which is why item_pack_contents names the rune itself rather than a cert.
// tradeable=no is dropped for the same reason as above - each pack's own wiki page says tradeable
// and noteable - and each gets a cert record.

[air_rune_pack]
name=Air rune pack
desc=A pack containing 100 air runes.
model=obj_air_rune_pack
2dzoom=1411
2dyan=2047
2dxof=-3
2dyof=-3
weight=4535g
cost=430
iop1=Open
category=item_pack
param=item_pack_contents,airrune
param=item_pack_amount,100

[cert_air_rune_pack]
certlink=air_rune_pack
certtemplate=template_for_cert

